WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.255
In this video, you will buy and sell your first coin.

00:00:03.255 --> 00:00:07.968
You will learn how to find a coin, how to check it, how to buy it, and how to sell it.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:10.106
We will practise with fake money first.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.989
Before anything else, look at the top right.

00:00:13.989 --> 00:00:15.900
This switch says Paper, or Live.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.171
Paper means practice, with fake money.

00:00:18.171 --> 00:00:19.485
Live means real money.

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:21.457
Keep it on Paper while you learn.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.507
Now, on the Hub, click Terminal.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:26.864
This is Discover.

00:00:26.864 --> 00:00:30.957
It shows coins as they launch, as they grow, and as they trend.

00:00:30.957 --> 00:00:32.321
Each box is one coin.

00:00:32.321 --> 00:00:34.400
Click any coin to open its page.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.414
We will open one as an example.

00:00:36.414 --> 00:00:38.233
This is not a tip to buy it.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.793
This is the coin page.

00:00:40.793 --> 00:00:42.942
The chart shows the price over time.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.150
Green candles mean the price went up.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.941
Red candles mean it went down.

00:00:46.941 --> 00:00:51.000
The buttons above it change the time, from one second to four hours.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:01:00.010
Across the top, you see the price, the market cap, which is what the whole coin is worth, how many people hold it, and how old it is.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:02.285
A dash means the app does not know yet.

00:01:02.285 --> 00:01:03.568
It does not mean zero.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:10.088
Under the chart, the Security tab shows warning signs, like a creator who already sold.

00:01:10.088 --> 00:01:12.994
The score, from zero to one hundred, sums it up.

00:01:12.994 --> 00:01:14.145
Red things are bad.

00:01:14.145 --> 00:01:16.869
But no score can promise that a coin goes up.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.852
Now the buy box, on the right.

00:01:19.852 --> 00:01:21.872
Make sure Buy is picked at the top.

00:01:21.872 --> 00:01:25.509
Click one of these amounts, or type your own amount in the box.

00:01:25.509 --> 00:01:27.299
This is how much SOL you spend.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:27.992
Start small.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.071
Then click the big green button.

00:01:31.071 --> 00:01:34.219
Right now it says Paper Buy, because we are practising.

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:37.481
In Live mode, it just says Buy, and it spends real money.

00:01:37.481 --> 00:01:40.400
The fees are shown just above it, before you click.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.330
To get out, click Sell at the top of the box.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.640
Pick how much to sell.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.783
One hundred percent sells all of it.

00:01:47.783 --> 00:01:49.331
Then click the red button.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.228
Under the buy box is Orders.

00:01:52.228 --> 00:01:53.935
Click New to set a stop loss.

00:01:53.935 --> 00:01:57.820
A stop loss sells for you if the price drops to a number you pick.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.234
A take profit sells when the price goes up to your number.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:02.999
Orders only work in Live mode.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:12.163
Last, the Trades page, in the menu on the left, shows every trade you made, and what you really made or lost, after every fee.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.123
That is it.

00:02:14.123 --> 00:02:15.678
Practise on Paper first.

00:02:15.678 --> 00:02:19.437
Start small, and decide when you will sell before you buy.

00:02:19.437 --> 00:02:23.973
Most new coins go to zero, so only trade money you can afford to lose.

00:02:23.973 --> 00:02:25.853
This is not financial advice.
